From: Codex <codex@openai.com>
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mt76: mt7996: flush NPU state for non-MLO station removal

Applies after the firmware's 0003 NPU station-removal patch to mt76
467ae2e3f190baf737e15e318906da0dc7d0ab91.

link_valid is initialized from sta->valid_links, so non-MLO clients skip
an NPU deletion placed exclusively in the link_valid block. Preserve the
existing MLO deletion path and also delete state when a non-MLO station
is finally removed (flush=true), before its WCID can be reused.

---
--- a/mt7996/main.c
+++ b/mt7996/main.c
@@ -1319,6 +1319,12 @@
 		mt7996_sta_deflink_release(dev, sta, link_id);
 		msta_link->wcid.link_valid = false;
 		msta->seclink_id = mt7996_sta_seclink_get(dev, msta);
+	} else if (flush && !sta->valid_links) {
+		/* Non-MLO stations have link_valid == false, but still own NPU
+		 * station state that must be invalidated before WCID reuse.
+		 */
+		mt76_npu_del_sta(&dev->mt76, msta_link->wcid.phy_idx,
+				 msta_link->wcid.idx);
 	}
 
 	if (flush) {
